From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:03:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/dtc: pylibfdt: use the Python 3 C API in the typemaps

Two typemaps in libfdt.i call PyString_FromString() and PyInt_AsLong().
Neither exists in Python 3; the build only ever worked because SWIG's
pyhead.swg defined them as macros onto the PyUnicode_/PyLong_ spellings
when targeting Python 3. SWIG 4.4 dropped that Python 2 compatibility
layer, so from SWIG 4.4 on the generated libfdt_wrap.c fails to compile:

  libfdt_wrap.c: In function '_wrap_fdt_next_node':
  libfdt_wrap.c:5618:20: error: implicit declaration of function
    'PyInt_AsLong'; did you mean 'PyLong_AsLong'?
  libfdt_wrap.c: In function '_wrap_fdt_get_property_by_offset':
  libfdt_wrap.c:6679:19: error: implicit declaration of function
    'PyString_FromString'; did you mean 'PyLong_FromString'?

along with the -Wint-conversion errors that follow from the implicit int
return type. That takes out scripts_dtc, so the build stops before it
reaches any board.

Call the Python 3 names directly. pylibfdt is Python 3 only - setup.py
is #!/usr/bin/env python3 and the Makefile invokes $(PYTHON3) - so no
version guard is needed, unlike the neighbouring typemaps that still
carry PY_VERSION_HEX tests for a Python 2 that cannot be reached here.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped b/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
index e4659489..c738d805 100644
--- a/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
+++ b/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
@@ -1033,7 +1033,7 @@ typedef uint32_t fdt32_t;
 	PyObject *buff;
 
 	if ($1) {
-		resultobj = PyString_FromString(
+		resultobj = PyUnicode_FromString(
 			fdt_string(fdt1, fdt32_to_cpu($1->nameoff)));
 		buff = PyByteArray_FromStringAndSize(
 			(const char *)($1 + 1), fdt32_to_cpu($1->len));
@@ -1070,7 +1070,7 @@ typedef uint32_t fdt32_t;
 
 /* typemaps used for fdt_next_node() */
 %typemap(in, numinputs=1) int *depth (int depth) {
-   depth = (int) PyInt_AsLong($input);
+   depth = (int) PyLong_AsLong($input);
    $1 = &depth;
 }
 
-- 
2.43.0

